# 3. CENTRAL GUARDIAN INTELLIGENCE HUB

Create or extend a single central intelligence layer named:

GUARDIAN CENTRAL INTELLIGENCE HUB (GCIH)

This will connect all existing security sections.

It must act as a common information exchange and intelligence-processing layer.

### Responsibilities

- Receive information from individual modules.
- Identify and normalise entities.
- Maintain shared intelligence records.
- Identify relationships between entities and events.
- Distribute relevant information to appropriate modules.
- Synchronise authorised intelligence across family devices.
- Trigger automatic reassessment when new information arrives.
- Update associated security incidents.
- Communicate relevant changes to the Smart Red Alert System.

### Important architectural distinction

The central intelligence hub must NOT replace individual detection engines.

Each section must retain its own detection logic.

For example:

- Call Scam remains responsible for analysing call-related activity.
- SMS Scam remains responsible for analysing messages.
- QR Scam remains responsible for QR-related analysis.
- Link Scam remains responsible for URL and domain analysis.
- Payment Safety remains responsible for payment-related analysis.

The central hub only coordinates, connects and distributes relevant information.

