# 18. REAL-WORLD ACCEPTANCE TESTS

The feature is not complete until the following scenarios work.

## Test 1: SMS to Call Scam

- A suspicious SMS contains a phone number.
- SMS Scam extracts and records it.
- Call Scam receives the relevant intelligence.
- The same number calls later.
- Call Scam displays the previous association.
- Its own risk engine reassesses the call.

## Test 2: QR to Payment Safety

- User scans a QR code.
- Guardian extracts a UPI ID.
- QR Scam displays the scan information.
- Payment Safety receives the UPI ID.
- Future payment-related analysis uses the shared indicator.

## Test 3: QR to Link Scam

- User scans a QR code containing a URL.
- QR Scam extracts the URL.
- Link Scam receives it automatically.
- Link Scam performs its own URL analysis.
- Both sections display relevant findings.

## Test 4: SMS to Link Scam

- A suspicious SMS contains a phishing URL.
- SMS Scam analyses the message.
- Link Scam receives the extracted URL.
- Link Scam performs independent domain and URL analysis.
- Related findings are connected.

## Test 5: Call, SMS and Payment Correlation

- Suspicious call detected.
- Related payment-request SMS received.
- Payment identifier extracted.
- Central intelligence identifies the shared entities.
- Behavioural analysis correlates the events.
- One incident is created or updated.
- Alert engine reassesses the incident.

## Test 6: Family-Wide Sharing

- Child's device detects a suspicious entity.
- Information is synchronised.
- Parent's device receives the permitted intelligence.
- Parent's relevant section updates.
- Parent's device discovers additional evidence.
- Updated intelligence synchronises back to the child.

## Test 7: Duplicate Prevention

- Same URL is discovered through SMS and QR.
- Guardian identifies the same entity.
- One entity record is maintained.
- Both source events are preserved.
- Relevant sections receive updates.
- Duplicate notifications are prevented.

## Test 8: False Positive Correction

- User marks an entity as legitimate.
- Guardian records the feedback.
- Relevant sections reassess their findings.
- The change synchronises across authorised devices.
- Original evidence is retained.

## Test 9: Offline Synchronisation

- Child's device loses internet connectivity.
- Local detection continues where supported.
- Events are queued securely.
- Internet connectivity returns.
- Events synchronise successfully.
- Duplicate records are not created.

## Test 10: Permission Revocation

- User revokes an Android permission.
- Guardian detects the unavailable capability.
- It stops claiming that the corresponding monitoring is active.
- Other functioning modules remain operational.

## Test 11: Family Privacy

- Two unrelated families use Guardian.
- One family detects a suspicious number.
- The other family must not receive that family's private event or incident data.

## Test 12: Existing Feature Regression

Verify that:

- Parent login still works.
- Child login still works.
- Family linking still works.
- Existing Call Watcher still works.
- Existing SMS functionality still works.
- QR scanning still works.
- Payment Safety still works.
- Link analysis still works.
- Existing notifications still work.
- Emergency Help still works.
- Existing Smart Red Alerts still work.
